has published reporting critical of Egyptian President Abdel-Fattah el-Sissi's government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>96% of world's coral reefs face critical risk of collapse, IUCN warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:010c70cdd5f6c1322f0560d0e525f5515484ba7431446272260d8a1fedd6421e</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T18:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/96-of-world-s-coral-reefs-face-critical-risk-of-collapse-iucn-warns/a-79736234--5504c1b3916f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/96-of-world-s-coral-reefs-face-critical-risk-of-collapse-iucn-warns/a-79736234?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Almost all of the world’s shallow-water coral reefs are at risk of collapse by 2075, with climate change the biggest threat. A new study found that 96% of reef systems are critically endangered.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's Mark Carney visits Turkey to boost trade ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ef471ee8507517998ccbebfea5e9774c9fdb58f58b9a4bba815aecf0dbbbbaf</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T17:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-s-mark-carney-visits-turkey-to-boost-trade-ties/a-79735039--dbd774d26d46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-s-mark-carney-visits-turkey-to-boost-trade-ties/a-79735039?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's the first bilateral visit by a Canadian prime minister to Turkey. Canada and Turkey upgraded their relations to a "strategic partnership" as Canada seeks to diversify trade beyond the US.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's Macron says 'illegitimate' protests will be banned in coming days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85411152dc6b8787a143da8b3e1c1cf4950968e30efcc6aab6fa19684f14dcac</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-macron-says-illegitimate-protests-will-be-banned-in-coming-days/a-79735137--c2dd52a04a07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-macron-says-illegitimate-protests-will-be-banned-in-coming-days/a-79735137?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron vowed to ban unauthorized protests after France was rocked by violence and looting. As anger over public services and the cost of living grows, authorities are bracing for more protests.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Are the French police the most violent in the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbd1acde3878edcb8bd7a54029c41bd208194680af74e928429f0ddd63495aa4</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-the-french-police-the-most-violent-in-the-eu/a-79732855--34f0b0f7045e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-the-french-police-the-most-violent-in-the-eu/a-79732855?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As protests continue in France, the French police are under scrutiny after new allegations of police brutality. The force has a bigger arsenal than most in Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran ready for another major US attack after midterm elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40b54439aba9a3da3c8ed7d8a8ae5a5c5918097f66bae0e98150a91f7c8d38f6</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-ready-for-another-major-us-attack-after-midterm-elections/a-79734082--65d965ab6d67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-ready-for-another-major-us-attack-after-midterm-elections/a-79734082?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian officials say the goal is to keep the regime in power and threaten enough regional costs to make a prolonged campaign unattractive. US media reports indicate that Trump is considering strikes after the midterms.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is EU putting profits over human rights in Vietnam?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2ec2db9feb73f8a3bc41c3f22b39e495df27f7f1e6e7af59b16f7f78ad42ae9</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-eu-putting-profits-over-human-rights-in-vietnam/a-79732812--0a31793443b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-eu-putting-profits-over-human-rights-in-vietnam/a-79732812?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU and Vietnam are deepening economic and diplomatic ties, but closer cooperation raises concerns about whether Brussels is doing enough to address Hanoi's human rights record, labor standards and trade imbalances.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Government expecting increased tax revenue in 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:656304364f4676baa8e48c9cbf829178bc7dcb1d91570e33ba09bfe2913f7cb9</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-government-expecting-increased-tax-revenue-in-2027/live-79728628--139a0de86753.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-government-expecting-increased-tax-revenue-in-2027/live-79728628?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finance Minister Lars Klingbeil said state tax revenue will increase by €4 billion in 2027. Meanwhile, public service websites have been coming back online after a PHP security scare.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Gandhi's nephew forced to pull protest photos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:174635ff9c001574f852ce1076db6a9e4e39babc9ab65cb7e4647412fbf74481</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-s-nephew-forced-to-pull-protest-photos/live-79727462--8042d9d73860.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-s-nephew-forced-to-pull-protest-photos/live-79727462?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The requested removal of "objectionable" photos from a cultural center took place in state run by Modi's BJP.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France confirms first Shamonda virus infection in a human death of 'severely immunocompromised' individual</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d838dfa2e96eef0c442855cf9565df49a5956e9ba7f0a8d19061173b74738796</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T12:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-confirms-first-shamonda-virus-infection-in-a-human-death-of-severely-immunocompromised-indivi/a-79731991--31f7ca31d255.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-confirms-first-shamonda-virus-infection-in-a-human-death-of-severely-immunocompromised-individual/a-79731991?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Shamonda virus has been detected in a human for the first time, French health officials said. Authorities see no risk to the public, adding that the victim, who died in early October, was severely immunocompromised.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's Balochistan border region sees growing unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:468252726aa85416bbf3aced5639cd24ee469c21b0cc817eed8260616f3dbf69</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-balochistan-border-region-sees-growing-unrest/a-79716399--7cda0ee86ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-balochistan-border-region-sees-growing-unrest/a-79716399?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Violence is on the rise in Iran's border region with Afghanistan and Pakistan. The Iran war could shift the strategic balance for militant groups operating in the area.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Life near the front line in Sloviansk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:162b820e74d9542dec0787e85fce2aa6d04d882cae0585542aa17304c3fe84ed</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636--5ef08a6d884a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russian continues to attack Sloviansk in eastern Ukraine, thousands of residents refuse to leave or struggle to find a way out. For many, poverty, family ties and beloved pets make evacuation painfully difficult.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany arrests Ukrainian man suspected of spying for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0342456949908cbd37535ce6b842d913dcc13f694a021af89a3437986f1d6432</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-arrests-ukrainian-man-suspected-of-spying-for-russia/a-79732373--a3202cca0fcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-arrests-ukrainian-man-suspected-of-spying-for-russia/a-79732373?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The suspect is thought to have gathered defense-related information on the production of tanks and munitions, as well as details about NATO's eastern flank.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU's Sakharov Prize won by the International Criminal Court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:678070911f5604c10c5da9cd77347e9d810ae593ccdcad4ec01d3cc17ea17e5c</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T10:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-sakharov-prize-won-by-the-international-criminal-court/a-79730914--66e722beb7e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-sakharov-prize-won-by-the-international-criminal-court/a-79730914?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU has announced the International Criminal Court as the winner of this year's Sakharov Prize. The annual prize is awarded to individuals and organizations for their work in supporting human rights and democracy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Germany overhaul its economy before AfD grows stronger?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b257f40fcacf0dbc8c2ca096b677f7b58fd69f1077b3c3b2c8f7523e68355e59</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-germany-overhaul-its-economy-before-afd-grows-stronger/a-79696102--b0df844ba99a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-germany-overhaul-its-economy-before-afd-grows-stronger/a-79696102?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflicts, rising costs and Chinese competition are testing Germany's economic model like never before. Which new sectors could revive growth and contain the far-right AfD, whose support has grown larger than ever?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4178a155c407ed7820c4ffa6c0dcdc47b65e4a9b251f9980ad7b611ebf296b80</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane is the clear front-runner for football's most prestigious individual prize, which will be awarded on Monday. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria: Concerns about security in the Black Sea dominate presidential election campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2d5c6b840c6812af23f835d2b701e9e39eae39a008cdae03a58c21337be0e3c</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094--fc0e44625feb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bulgaria's presidential election campaign has been shaped by recent drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea and the government's reduced support for Ukraine, making foreign policy a key factor in the first round.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa CDC calls crisis meeting as Ebola spreads</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f9348253fbc6319832c38b958c8bdfc4ac21d648a95eb3eb8b2186ec7519d32</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-cdc-calls-crisis-meeting-as-ebola-spreads/a-79728604--521b9bc7db1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-cdc-calls-crisis-meeting-as-ebola-spreads/a-79728604?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">African health officials will hold a crisis meeting as the Ebola outbreak spreads from Congo to neighboring countries and beyond. The "extraordinary virtual meeting" will convene on October 28.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU moves to loosen rules on pesticide use as experts sound the alarm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a28f16933e84e9d4e761d6c0148882b1d22aaa3344c6a87711d52c4d808ea56</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422--0c5446a2b9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants to relax rules for pesticides, saying it will be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia trade strikes after Witkoff talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04db67e1db2ab3027d22b006ee110006b0edf84cfafdf0be78a11f62bd5c220e</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T04:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-trade-strikes-after-witkoff-talks/a-79727542--9a5da82ad2b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-trade-strikes-after-witkoff-talks/a-79727542?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Soon after Putin and Zelenskyy expressed willingness to resume US-mediated talks, Russia and Ukraine traded major attacks on each other's capitals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
